Practical 1

Example 1: Create a Simple ASP.NET Core Web Application

Step 1: Open Visual Studio 2019
● Launch Visual Studio 2019.
● Click Create a new project.
Step 2: Select Project Template
● Search for ASP.NET Core Web App.
● Select it.
● Click Next.
Step 3: Configure Project
● Project Name: HelloWebApp
● Location: Choose a folder
● Click Create
Step 4: Choose Framework
● Select .NET Core
● Select desired framework version
● Choose Web Application (Model-View-Controller) or Empty
● Click Create
Visual Studio creates the project automatically.
Example 2: Display "Hello World"
Open:
Controllers/HomeController.cs
Modify the action:
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
  public class HomeController : Controller
  {
    public IActionResult Index()
    {
      return Content("Hello World from ASP.NET Core!");
    }
  }
}
Save the file.
Step 5: Run the Application
Press:
F5
or click:
IIS Express
Browser opens automatically.

Output:
Hello World from ASP.NET Core!
Example 3: Create a Simple Form
HomeController
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
  public class HomeController : Controller
  {
    public IActionResult Index()
    {
      return View();
    }
    [HttpPost]
    public IActionResult Index(string name)
    {
      ViewBag.Message = "Welcome " + name;
      return View();
    }
  }
}
Create View
Open:
Views/Home/Index.cshtml
Replace contents:
<form method="post">
  <label>Name:</label>
  <input type="text" name="name" />
  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>
@if(ViewBag.Message != null)
{
  <h2>@ViewBag.Message</h2>
}
Run application.
Enter a name and click Submit.
Output:
Welcome John

